  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Course Atlas",
    "overview": "Every screen is a map of the learner's journey: where they are, how far they have come, and the one next step. Structure is the design. Program, course, module and topic nest in a fixed order; progress bars, step markers and dates are the landmarks; the page around them stays quiet so the landmarks read at a glance. The same map serves the platform pages (Dashboard, My Learning, course and program pages, Calendar) and the player, where the content itself takes the space and the chrome recedes.\n\nThe atlas is printed for many partners. A skin changes the brand colours (SKO teal, Gold, Red, and the Sea proposal), never the structure, the components or the type. Light and dark themes, a colour-vision-safe mode and a text scale up to 130 % sit on top of every skin, and each combination holds WCAG 2.2 AA. Density is moderate: generous 44 px targets on phones, 16 px card padding, one content column of 1200 px on desktop.\n\nComponents are firm and welcoming: large, honest targets, direct labels, and one small moment of warmth, the yellow spark that the primary button turns to on hover. Depth is light and hybrid: the default skin separates surfaces with hairline borders and tonal steps; the Sea skin trades those borders for a soft teal shadow. Gradients are off-brand everywhere.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Role tokens only: every colour, radius and type style comes from a DS role, never a raw value.",
      "One accent at a time: teal for action and position, yellow only as the hover spark and for warnings.",
      "Progress is blue; green means done, and comes with an icon and a word.",
      "Radius by what an element is, not by its size, with the nesting rule inner + padding = outer.",
      "The same content on desktop, tablet and phone; layouts change, content does not hide."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Role Token Rule",
        "body": "No raw hex in a component. Every colour is a `--color-*` role (`bg-sko-*`, `text-sko-*`, `border-sko-*`), so a skin, theme or vision mode can re-point it. The token lint (`pnpm lint:tokens`) fails the build otherwise.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
